{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed a stuck Kafka consumer and submitted the mitigation (the endpoint returned 200).\n\n**Cause:** the `orders-validator` consumer stopped at offset 20 of `orders-fulfillment`. That record was truncated JSON (`{\"order_id\":\"ORD-100020\",\"amount\":`). The consumer pauses on any record it can't validate, so every order after it went unprocessed, and lag grew to 17.\n\n**Fix:** I scaled `orders-validator` to 0 and reset its consumer group to offset 21, which skips the bad record. I then scaled it back to 1. It now processes new orders normally, with offsets past 54 and no errors.\n\n**Side effects:** the skipped record was not reprocessed, and nothing was done to the producer or the topic. The earlier frontend and checkout connection errors were from the pods restarting at the start of my investigation, and I didn't look into them further.\n\nI haven't confirmed that end-user requests are succeeding. The submission triggers that validation."}}
